<lines>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_1">82 Etiam legale pretium auget affectio.</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_2">83 Tertia causa augendi pretium est prae¬</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_3">praestantia mercis.</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_4">84 Sicut etiam deterior merces minuit.</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_5">pretium.</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_6">85 Quarta causa est periculum non</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_7">soluendi in vendente.</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_8">86 Quinta causa periculum non soluen¬</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_9">di mercem in emente.</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_10">87 Obijcitur, &amp; soluitur.</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_11">88 Certum est periculum hoc esse pretio</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_12">aestimabile.</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_13">89 Cautè taxandum periculum, &amp; parui.</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_14">90 Sexta causa augendi est asportatio</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_15">ad alium locum.</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_16">91 Duobus modis potestántelligi.</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_17">92. Res hic existens quomodo possit ven¬</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_18">di pretio existentis alibi</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_19">93 Is qui merces aliò erat translaturus</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_21">illius loci pretio potest vendere,</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_22">&amp; pretium hic augere.</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_23">94 Emptores lanarum minoris multis</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_24">titulis excusantur.</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_25">95 Septima causa pretium augendi est.</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_26">donatio liberalis.</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_27">96 Certum est veram donationem non</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_28">solùm minuere, sed omnino tol¬</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_29">lere pretium.</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_30">97 Donationem pretium minuere Do¬</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_31">ctores asserunt</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_32">98 Quando vis, aut dolus intercedit do¬</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_33">natio non praesumitur.</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_34">99 Ignorantia donationem excludit.</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_35">100 Amici consanguinei, &amp; sodales prae¬</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_36">sumuntur donare.</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_37">101 Octaua causa est modus vendendi</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_38">explicandus.</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_39">DIrimus quae pretium ordinatium,</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_40">&amp; currens in rep. non tam augent,</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_42">quam constituunt; quia cum semper cum</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_43">pretio communi coniuncta sint, com¬</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_44">mune pretium non variatur ex illis, sed</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_45">ex illis consurgit, quod ideo naturale</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_46">vocatur: in taxa verò, quia semper in¬</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_47">terueniunt, semper sunt attendenda,</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_48">sicut in pretio etiam conuentionali, at¬</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_49">que adeo hoc etiam pretium consti¬</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_50">tuunt, si instè definiantur. Dicamus iam de</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_51">ijs, quae pretijs ordinarijs accidunt, vtil¬</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_52">la vel augeant vel minuant, non semper, sed¬</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_53">quando eueniunt. Quę disceptatio ad tol¬</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_54">lendas hinc fraudes, de scrupulos valde</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_55">vtilis est. Sunt ergo aliqua, quae pretium</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_56">vulgare, &amp; ordinarium in rep. constitu¬</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_57">tum, siua legale, siue naturale augendo,</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_58">vel minuendo variant.</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_59">Primum est damnum emergens, vel</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_60">lucrum cessans duo fulmina belli scho¬</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_61">larum, seu vt melius dicam, duo vasa</line>
</lines>
